       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" data-account-id=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" accountid=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Jared Whiklo</a>, indeed, fcrepo-camel-webapp does not support (or at least it does not work) making authorized requests. As a result of not wanting to maintain two redundant implementations, we will be moving away from fcrepo-camel-webapp <span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> towards the Karaf/OSGi deployment of the Camel machinery.<br/>\nThanks for the good catch, however.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-1691\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-1691</a></p>",
